    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d891">

                <pb facs="0958" n="1792" xml:id="pg1792"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72111/7065a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Netherlands</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Garrett</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-31T18:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 31, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1825. Please ascertain and report by cable as soon as possible attitude of
                    Netherlands Government towards American merchantmen defensively armed which may
                    enter Netherlands colonial ports. Such merchantmen ordinarily carry a 5.40-inch
                    gun mounted aft and a three pounder forward. Guns manned by regular Navy crew of
                    from 18 to 21 men.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
